```

```mdl
feat F-22: The feature map in a project
  req F-22.1: A feature's `spec:` field cites the spec that breaks it down, so specs nest to any depth. Breaking a
              feature down (`CodeOperation.CreateSpec` with `breaks`) makes a spec with the software package in the
              owner project and cites it, or returns the spec the feature already cites.
  req F-22.3: On a project's Specs tab, a double-click on a feature with a breakdown, or the companion's "Break down",
              picks the breakdown in the spec picker, where it nests by citation (org.dxos.plugin.projects#F-4.6);
              a feature with none gets one first. Elsewhere the breakdown opens as an article of its own.
  req F-22.4: This plugin provides one dialect, the software dialect (`org.dxos.spec.software`), which extends the
              code, app, plugin, QA and SQL dialects. A spec that uses it is offered Data model, API and Board in
