      expect: the canvas draws the spec's clusters again
    - name: Open the launch video
      do: Open the Structure tab, then pick "Launch video" from the spec dropdown.
      expect: Definitions draws the script's clusters, around maya and around narrator, and Structure offers only
        Definitions and Related
    - name: Open a character's cluster
      do: Double-click the maya cluster.
      expect: a frame per scene holding what only it names, SC-2 marked as opening a level
    - name: Open a scene
      do: Double-click SC-2.
      expect: SC-2 is centred, with the scenes and screenings that name it and the shots, lines and cast it names
    - name: Press a scene
      do: Pick Related, then press SC-3's form.
      expect: Related centres on SC-3
    - name: Open the script's decisions
      do: Open the Decisions tab and pick Ledger.
      expect: a card per block the script's two decisions affect
```

```mdl
test QA-8: Read a spec as text and as forms, then tour its companion tabs
  desc: |
    The spec as plain text, then as a form per block, with a requirement added and dragged to the top, a dependency
    picked, a status picked, a type's field switched and an input added to an operation; then, still as forms, every view of the spec's companion
    tabs, in order: Structure's Definitions and Related, with Related following the card pressed from block to block, then the software dialect's Data model, API and Board; Decisions at the
    cursor and the Ledger, a level at a time; Review, and the software dialect's Code. Definitions, Related,
    Decisions and Review are plugin-projects' (its F-6, F-7 and F-8).
    A script in the video dialect then offers only the views that read any dialect, and Definitions drills into it as
    it does into code.
    Walked by the autocue flow `spec-companions` against Composer.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-20.1, F-20.4, F-22.4]
  status: passing            # 2026-11-06, recorded by autocue/spec-companions.mjs
  given:
    - composer serves plugin-code and plugin-video, enabled
    - the project "Composer specs" owns the spec "CodePlugin", whose text is this spec and which uses the software
      dialect, with the review of 2026-10-27
      (`containers/SpecArticle/__fixtures__/plugin-code.review-2026-10-27.mdl`) recorded against it, and five of
      its features given a status, at least one per status
    - the project also owns "Launch video", whose text is deus's `lang/examples/launch-video.mdl` and which uses
      plugin-video's Video package
    - the Specs tab shows "CodePlugin" as plain text with the cursor on its first line, the sidebar closed and the
      companion 62rem wide
  steps:
    - name: Read the spec as text
      do: Scroll the spec down and back.
      expect: the title and description, then the plugin block and the blocks after it as MDL text
    - name: Switch to the forms
      do: Pick Markdown in the toolbar's view menu.
      expect: each block drawn as a form, the plugin block headed by CodePlugin with its purpose under it
    - name: Add a requirement
      do: Press F-4's form, then the add button at the top right of its requirements, and type a requirement.
      expect: a row labelled F-4.7 holding the text
    - name: Move it to the top
      do: Drag the new requirement's handle above F-4.1.
      expect: the new requirement is labelled F-4.1, and the others follow it
    - name: Pick a feature it depends on
      do: Open F-4's Depends picker and pick F-1.
      expect: Depends shows F-1
    - name: Set a feature's status
      do: Pick Prototype in F-4's status tag.
      expect: the tag shows Prototype with its icon, in the status's hue
    - name: Edit a type's field
      do: Press CodeProject's form, flip the first field's Optional switch and open its Type list.
      expect: the switch flips, and the list offers the spec's types
    - name: Add an operation's input
      do: Press verifySpec's form, add an input, name it strict, pick boolean as its type and switch it to optional.
      expect: verifySpec's inputs hold spec and strict, strict a boolean marked optional
    - name: Open Definitions
      do: Open the companion's Structure tab.
      expect: Definitions draws a card per cluster
    - name: Open a cluster
      do: Double-click the CoderSkill cluster.
      expect: a frame per feature holding what only it names
    - name: Open Related
      do: Pick Related in Structure's toolbar.
      expect: Related centres on CodeProject, the block at the cursor
    - name: Press a feature
      do: Press F-8's form.
      expect: Related centres on F-8, with what it names below it and QA-1 as what checks it
    - name: Press the next feature
      do: Press F-9's form.
      expect: Related centres on F-9
    - name: Press a type
      do: Press CodeProject's form.
      expect: Related centres on CodeProject, with the features naming it above it
    - name: Open Data model
      do: Pick Data model in Structure's toolbar.
      expect: the spec's types and their fields
    - name: Open API
      do: Pick API in Structure's toolbar.
      expect: the spec's operations, with the services each needs
    - name: Open Board
      do: Pick Board in Structure's toolbar.
      expect: a column per status, the spec's features sorted into them
    - name: Open Decisions at the cursor
      do: Click into F-20.4's text in F-20's form, then open the companion's Decisions tab.
      expect: At cursor shows the decisions that hold on F-20.4, then those that hold on F-20
    - name: Open the Ledger
      do: Pick Ledger in Decisions' toolbar.
      expect: a card per block, the most recently decided first, under a count of the decisions not yet approved
    - name: Open a block
      do: Click the SpecViewContent card.
      expect: its threads, a card each, with an approve button on those holding unapproved decisions
    - name: Open a thread
      do: Click the first thread.
      expect: the approve button at the top, what holds now, then the thread's decisions by day
    - name: Open Review
      do: Open the companion's Review tab.
      expect: the review's summary, a count per status and a card per verdict
    - name: Open Code
      do: Show the done verdicts, then open compileEntry from buildProject's verdict menu.
      expect: Code shows `compiler/build.ts` with compileEntry highlighted
    - name: Open the launch video
      do: Pick "Launch video" from the spec dropdown, then open Structure's Definitions.
      expect: the script's clusters, around maya and around narrator, and Structure offers no Data model, API or Board
    - name: Open a character's cluster
      do: Double-click the maya cluster.
      expect: a frame per scene holding what only it names
    - name: Open a scene
      do: Double-click SC-2.
      expect: SC-2 is centred, with its shots, voiceover, caption and cast and the screenings that name it
    - name: Press a scene
      do: Pick Related, then press SC-3's form.
      expect: Related centres on SC-3
    - name: Open the script's decisions
      do: Open the Decisions tab and pick Ledger.
      expect: a card per block the script's two decisions affect
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Specs sync both ways with their files in a local checkout, in the desktop app and in a Composer dev server, through one shared file service; Composer is the spec viewer.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: A synced spec references its original location by the key `github:<owner>/<repo>/<path>`. The checkout is found in a predictable place: a list of repositories in settings, or the working directory.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14.2, Settings]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: A spec can reference blocks of other specs, and the spec's existing visualizations show those blocks as boxes on the graph.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-15.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: An agent skill reviews a spec's compliance and produces a review; the spec viewer annotates the spec with the status from the latest review.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Specs reference code symbols as `github:<owner>/<repo>/<path>#<Symbol>`; double-click or Ctrl-click navigates to the symbol.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-15.2, F-15.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The key is stored in the Spec's meta keys as { source: github.com/<owner>/<repo>, id: <path> } and written in text with the `github:` prefix. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14]
  why: plugin-projects and plugin-debug already key imported specs this way, so those specs sync with no migration.
  rejected: A new `source` field on Spec; a single `github:` source string with the repo in the id.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: Sync polls every 2 seconds and reconciles three-way against the last agreed text; with no base or on conflict the file wins. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14.3]
  why: Polling is one code path for Tauri and the dev route; the repository is where specs are reviewed and versioned, so it wins ties.
  rejected: Tauri's fs watch plus a dev-server websocket (two mechanisms); Composer winning conflicts.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: The dev route reads only inside the workspace root and `DX_SPEC_ROOTS`, and writes only `.mdl` files; the desktop app adds no Tauri command and uses the fs plugin's existing scope. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-14.1, F-14.5]
  why: The route is reachable by any page that can hit localhost, so it is no wider than a spec sync needs.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: A source key with a fragment names a spec block or a code symbol by the file's extension; the graph draws both as dashed external boxes, and the Code view shows the file at the symbol inside the spec page. Fills in [D-3] and [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-15]
  why: Showing code beside the spec keeps the spec page the IDE; VS Code is one button away where the host knows the path.
  rejected: Symbol lookup through introspect-mcp, which is node-only and indexes by package rather than by file.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: A review is a `<SPEC>.review.mdl` beside the spec with one `verdict` per item, statuses done, untested, partial, diverged and missing; a feature shows the worst status of its requirements. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16]
  why: An `.mdl` file reuses the parser, syncs through the same file service, and diffs in review like the spec.
  rejected: A JSON sidecar; a section inside the spec, which would make every review a spec change.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Links from a spec to the code that implements it are not part of the spec. They are annotations from another source, rendered as decorations in the editor, the same as the decision chips.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-5
  affects: [SpecArticle, F-15, F-16.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-12: The annotation source is the latest review: each verdict's evidence keys become chips on the item's declaration line and dashed code boxes on the definitions graph, and both open the Code view at the symbol. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.5, F-15.3]
  why: A review already maps each item to its code with checked evidence keys, so no second index is needed and the links stay current with each review.
  rejected: A separate code-map sidecar file; a symbol index built from the code.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Every leaf node is a card or an article, so users meet the same anatomy everywhere (an icon, a menu top right); cards are hosted by one of four containers (masonry, canvas, kanban, list) that share navigation, selection, highlighting, reactivity and scrolling, and each container has a storybook with fixtures. A review verdict is such a card.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-14: A verdict is a VerdictCard (status icon, item id, menu: show in spec, open code) in the list container (Mosaic stack); its stories use the real plugin-file-system review as their fixture. Fills in [D-13].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.4]
  why: The list container already provides keyboard navigation and a current item that can follow the spec; a real review exercises every status.
  rejected: One read-only form per verdict, which gave every verdict three labelled rows and no menu.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: Local file access is the `service SpecFs` (read, write, list, roots) with its two backends; the operations that touch local files, op:importSpec and op:listLocalSpecs, sit on top of it and declare `requires: [SpecFs]`.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [SpecFs, importSpec, listLocalSpecs, F-14.1]
  why: The code already has one SpecFs with a Tauri and a dev-route backend; a service block states that contract once instead of in each operation.
  rejected: Separate read/write/list operations, which would expose raw file access as agent tools.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: Approve [D-15].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
```

```mdl
decision D-17: A Composer plugin is declared with a `plugin` block (`lang/plugin.mdl`): prose on what it is for and the list of modules it adds. A plugin spec opens with it, directly after the frontmatter; this spec declares `plugin CodePlugin`.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodePlugin]
  why: MDL had no plugin ext; the plugin was implied by the document, so its modules could not be described, reviewed or linked to.
  rejected: Capabilities, activation events and requirements per module — left to the code until the dialect grows.
```

```mdl
decision D-18: Beside each reviewed item the editor shows one chip row from the review: the status, the code that covers the item (or "no code"), and tested or untested.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-16.5]
  why: Status, coverage and testing are one judgement about one item; separate rows of chips read as unrelated, and the old chips had low contrast.
```

```mdl
decision D-19: Spec sync uses the generic file-system service in plugin-file-system (github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file-system/PLUGIN.mdl#FileSystem); plugin-code's own `service SpecFs` is removed, op:importSpec and op:listLocalSpecs require the shared service, and its dev route is `/__dx/fs` with extra roots in `DX_FS_ROOTS`.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-15
  affects: [importSpec, listLocalSpecs, F-14.1]
  why: File access is not specific to specs; one service serves every plugin and the general-dev direction.
```

```mdl
