```mdl
decision D-59: A section embedded in a spec is compact and folds like an outline. Icons sit in a gutter column: the fold chevron on the header row, and under it each requirement's check, the `+` of "Add requirement" and the "Needs" row's arrow. The header row reads chevron, block id and name, with the name in the form's `title` presentation and the status as a `pill` at the row's end, as ProjectArticle draws them. The description has no label, uses the `plain` presentation and shows when it has text or the section has attention. Requirements have no label and no field well until focused; their remove and add actions show while the section has attention. Folded, only the header row shows, with the requirement count beside the status and the needed features as tags after the name. Which sections are folded is kept on the device, not synced.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-20.10, F-20.11, QA-4]
  why: A user reported that a section with five requirements was about 550 px tall, so a screen held 1.5 features and the spec was unusable for them.
```

```mdl
decision D-60: The compact section creates no new form components. It composes the existing `Form` presentations, fields and fieldsets, `ObjectMultiPicker`, react-ui `Card`, `Layout`, `Tag` and `Icon`, and `RequirementEditor`. A behaviour that composition cannot give is a gap to raise, fixed in the existing primitive only with the user's agreement. Fills in [D-59].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-20.11]
  why: Sections should look and behave like every other form in the app.
  rejected:
    - A new field renderer, a hand-built form, or a section-specific wrapper around the inputs.
```

```mdl
decision D-61: react-ui-form's `MarkdownField` draws the `title` and `plain` presentations in place, with no well and one line that grows with its text, as `TextField` does. The description placeholder is one line. The "Needs" picker stays in place whatever has attention, so several features can be picked in a row. Fills in [D-60].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-20.11]
  why: A feature's description is markdown, and `MarkdownField` drew a six-line well for every presentation.
```

```mdl
decision D-62: The "Needs" row is an `ObjectMultiPicker` over the feature's `DependsOn` targets, and each pick or removal runs `AddFeatureDependency` or `RemoveFeatureDependency`. Its options leave out the feature and every feature that depends on it, directly or through others. The fold state is `CodeCapabilities.State.collapsed`, keyed by feature id, in a local store under `org.dxos.plugin.code.state`. `RequirementEditor` renders a section of its host's grid card, so its icons share the host's rail. Fills in [D-59] and [D-61].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-20.11]
  why: Dependencies are relations edited through operations, not a field of the feature, so the picker is mounted beside the form rather than through it. Leaving out the features that would close a cycle means the operation never has to refuse a pick.
  rejected:
    - Read-only tags while the section lacks attention, which replaced the picker as soon as attention moved and hid how to add another feature.
```

```mdl
decision D-63: A folded section names the features it needs by block id (`F-2`), not by name. The ids sit with the requirement count at the end of the header row, spaced as the ids are from each other. Fills in [D-59].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-20.11]
  why: Names made a folded row long; block ids keep it compact.
```

```mdl
decision D-64: The status at the end of the header row uses react-ui-form's `tag` presentation, which is what [D-59]'s `pill` is called since `pill` was renamed to `tag`. Fills in [D-59].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-20.11]
  why: The presentation was renamed under this change; the look D-59 chose is the same.
