  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8, F-22.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-117: Only the dialects a file's `extends` names become the spec's dialects; the specs it extends stay in the file, and a push writes `extends` with the spec's dialects and those specs. Fills in [D-116].
  date: 2026-11-09
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: `extends` names other specs too (a plugin spec extends the spec it builds on), which are not dialects and would read the spec as one that names no known dialect.
  rejected: Storing the whole `extends` list in `dialects`, which reads a spec that extends only another spec with no dialect at all.
```

```mdl
decision D-118: A file whose `extends` names no dialect is read with the software dialect, on import and on every pull, as a plugin's bundled spec is. Fills in [D-116]; supersedes [D-115].
  date: 2026-11-09
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-115
  affects: [F-14.8, F-22.4]
  why: The specs in a checkout that name no dialect are plugin specs, and a pull that kept the old dialects would let the field and the file disagree.
  rejected: Reading such a file with the core and changelog dialects only, which drops the views and blocks a plugin spec uses.
```

```mdl
decision D-119: Finish the one store for a spec's dialects: one Deus rule maps a file to its dialects for imports, pulls and `deus lint`; a migration moves the front matter left in older specs' text into their fields; a push writes no `extends` for a spec whose dialects are unset; the editor reads the same dialects as the views.
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8, F-22.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-120: A spec's empty `dialects` is unset: a push leaves the file's `extends` as it is, and a pull fills it from the file. Fills in [D-119].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: Specs made in Composer, and specs imported before [D-116], hold no dialects, and the sync writes every bound spec's file on each pass, so writing their empty list put `extends: []` into files nobody had edited.
  rejected: Writing `extends: []`, which a file reads as naming no dialect, and so as software.
```

```mdl
decision D-121: A pull takes from the front matter only the keys and the dialects the file changed since the last sync. Fills in [D-119].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: A dialect turned on in Composer and not yet pushed was turned off again by the next pull of a file that had not changed, and every pull rewrote the field, rebuilding the editor.
  rejected: Taking the whole front matter on every pull, which loses local changes the text merge keeps.
```

```mdl
decision D-122: The `Spec` 0.4.0 migration takes the front matter of a spec whose text starts with one into its fields, as an import does, and leaves the text after it; a spec that already names dialects keeps them. Fills in [D-119].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: Specs imported before [D-116] kept their front matter in their text and named no dialects, so the views and the editor read them with no dialect.
  rejected: Reading a spec's dialects from its text's front matter when its field is empty, which keeps two stores.
```

```mdl
decision D-123: The editor checks a spec's references to itself, and finds the links it names, by the id in its meta, which its text no longer holds. Fills in [D-119].
