```mdl
decision D-132: Deus reads front matter with `yaml`'s failsafe schema, so every value is a string, and writes it by editing the parsed document: a changed value is set in place, keeping its comment, a list keeps its style, and a value is quoted where YAML needs it. Front matter that does not parse reads as none and is written back as it is. Fills in [D-131].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: The core schema reads `version: 1.0` as the number 1; rewriting whole lines dropped comments and turned list-style `extends` into inline lists.
```

```mdl
decision D-133: Deus reads front matter with `yaml`'s failsafe schema, so every value is a string. Front matter that is not a readable YAML map (a YAML error or warning, an unresolved alias, a block that is a scalar or a list) reads as unreadable, which is not the same as none: a pull or fill takes nothing from it, and an edit returns it as it is. An edit replaces only the source of the values it sets, keeping every other byte, the comments on a list it rewrites and the lines of the items that stay, and quotes a value as the core schema needs. Fills in [D-131].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-132
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: Reading such a block as none set a spec's dialects to software on a pull, and re-serialising the document on every edit rewrote lines nobody changed and dropped the comments on `extends`.
  rejected: Editing the parsed document and serialising it whole, which normalises indentation, spacing and folded text.
```

```mdl
decision D-134: A spec whose text keeps its front matter takes every field from its file on every sync pass, not only the fields it has unset. Fills in [D-119].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: Such a text is the file, so a field filled once kept its first value while the file's front matter changed.
```

```mdl
decision D-135: Writing `extends` compares the list the file has with the one it would write, so an id the spec lists that this build does not know is written once. Fills in [D-119].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: Such an id was kept from the file as a spec it extends and added again as a dialect, so the list grew on every pass.
```

```mdl
decision D-136: Each sync pass first moves front matter at the start of a spec's text into its fields, as the migration does, and reads the text once; only front matter that does not parse stays in the text, which then syncs as it is and fills only unset fields. Fills in [D-119].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-134
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: Taking every field from a text-held front matter on every pass undid renames, attached dialects and toggles made in Composer; with the front matter in the fields there is one store.
  rejected: Having each writer of a field move the text's front matter first, which leaves every writer that forgets it to be undone.
```

```mdl
decision D-137: An edit to front matter splices each value into its source: a scalar up to the end of its content, a list keeping the lines of the items that stay (an item with an `@version` matches its id) and the lines between them, adding new items after them, a new key on its own line at the end. A value is quoted where a YAML 1.1 or 1.2 reader would take it for anything but a string, and is never a block scalar. When the result does not read back as the edits on the block's other values, the edited document is written whole; when that does not either, the block is left as it is. Front matter that is not a readable YAML map reads as unreadable, not as none. Fills in [D-131].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-133
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: Splicing past a block value's line break joined the next key onto it, rebuilding a list span dropped comment lines between items, and a key appended to a flow map made the block unreadable; checking the read-back catches the layouts a splice cannot handle.
```

```mdl
decision D-138: A pull against a last synced file whose front matter does not parse takes only the fields the spec has unset. Fills in [D-119].
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-14.8]
  why: Read as no fields, such a base made every field the fixed file holds look changed, so a rename made while the file was broken was lost.
```

```mdl
decision D-139: Front matter is written by the `yaml` library, which writes the whole block; Composer does no splicing of its own.
  date: 2026-11-13
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-137
  affects: [F-14.8]
