```mdl
decision D-141: Front matter at the start of a spec's text that parses and names its `id`, `name`, `version` or `extends` is an edit made in Composer: each sync pass, GitHub import and GitHub export moves it into the fields, taking every value it sets, and where the last synced file's front matter does not parse, writes the moved block in its place. A block that names none of those keys is the text's own. A pull into a text whose front matter does not parse takes a file whose front matter parses into the fields and writes only its body to the text. Fills in [D-119].
