```

```mdl
decision D-143: A file's first block is its front matter, whatever it holds, and a spec's text is always what follows it. No sync pass, GitHub import or GitHub export reads front matter from the text: a block at the start of the text is part of the text, written after the file's front matter, and sets no field. Front matter that does not parse stays in the file, and the spec's field changes wait until it is fixed there. A file synced without front matter gets a block from the fields when its text starts with one. Fills in [D-119] and [D-225].
