```mdl
decision D-155: A spec's features are the `feat` blocks of its text. Feature objects are gone: the board and the companion read the blocks through plugin-projects' `useSpecBlocks`, and edits go through `SetSpecBlock` and `DeleteSpecBlock`. The feature operations (`CreateFeature`, `UpdateFeature`, `DeleteFeature`, `AddFeatureDependency`, `RemoveFeatureDependency`, `LinkFeatureTask`, `GetFeatures`, `ImportSpecFeatures`, `ExportSpecFeatures`, `ImportFeatureLinks`) give way to `CreateSpec` with `breaks`, `UpdateSpec`, `LinkTask` and `CreateShowcase` with `items`. Tasks and showcases link to a feature by block key, through `SpecItem.Implements` and `Showcase.Demonstrates` with `item`. The feature embeds, `/feature` and the spec codec are removed, so a spec syncs with its file as text, and a breakdown nests in the nav tree by citation instead of through feature levels. QA-4 and QA-6, which walked the embeds, are removed, and the Board reads the blocks. Replaces [D-57], [D-62] and [D-111].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-19, F-20, F-21, F-22, QA-4, QA-5]
  why: Two stores for one feature drifted apart. With the text as the only store, the spec, its file and every view agree by construction, and the schema-driven block forms edit every block kind the same way.
  rejected: Keeping feature objects as a cache of the blocks, which keeps the sync that drifted.
```

